problem_statement_fixed:
The networking subsystem provides multicast route lookups by group address only (net_route_mcast_lookup). A caller cannot determine whether a given multicast group has a route associated with a specific network interface. The system needs a new public API named net_route_mcast_lookup_by_iface with the signature:

struct net_route_entry_mcast *net_route_mcast_lookup_by_iface(struct in6_addr *group, struct net_if *iface);

It should look up a multicast routing entry by both the IPv6 multicast group address and a specific interface, returning a pointer to the matching struct net_route_entry_mcast entry, or NULL if no entry exists for that combination. A matching entry is one whose multicast route group prefix matches the supplied IPv6 multicast group address and whose associated interface set includes the supplied interface.
